            "review_title": "Review at The Never Ending Summer",
            "review_text": "Tiffany Le\n1 contribution\n0\nA hidden gem\nJun 2020\nThis restaurant is located in the middle of District 10, on Vĩnh Viễn (which means \"never ending\") street. It is small and cozy; therefore, it is not suitable for large groups.\n\nI have been to The Never Ending Summer six times already, and it has always been my go-to. The food is nicely cooked and beautifully decorated - you may be led into thinking that they serve humble helpings but the reality proves the opposite. \n\nThe waiters are amazing! They are friendly, helpful, and attentive; and they even go to great lengths to remember familiar guests' faces. I do find this pretty pleasing as it makes my dining experience so much better.\n\nThe price is reasonable in regard to the above quality in their servings. For the regular menu, the price ranges from 69k to 99k; for the signature menu, it may be 100k+. There is a variety of drinks to choose from, which is another bonus point for this amazing location.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten June 13, 2020",
